  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA-only, singleprofile, PCA_n2000) yielded only 48.5% accuracy, a weak baseline that provides little guidance on which design axis (modality, encoder, profile, aggregation) will be most impactful. Uncertainty: We have no information about whether the image modality carries complementary or superior signal for this task. Question tested: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, ResNet50) isolates the effect of modality while holding profile setting constant at singleprofile, directly comparing image features against the RNA-only baseline. Why this is the best next experiment: Knowing whether image features are informative (and at what level) is the most consequential strategic fork—determining whether to invest remaining budget in multimodal fusion configs or to focus on improving RNA representations. A strong image-only result would justify exploring multimodal configs (016-051); a similarly weak result would redirect effort toward better RNA encoders (scvi, scgpt) and multiprofile aggregation. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the highest-leverage design choice with 8 experiments remaining."
}

